    "text": {
      "en": "Stands at Korkiakangas in Utajärvi, east of Oulu, and covers the Oulu region of northern Finland. The site has been in use since 1997; its dual-polarisation radar went into service in autumn 2013 and maps precipitation up to about 250 km away."
